Place one pointer `left` at index 0 and `right` at the last index `len(nums) - 1`:
```python
while left < right:
    current_sum = nums[left] + nums[right]
    if current_sum == target:
        return [left, right]
    elif current_sum < target:
        left += 1  # need a larger sum
    else:
        right -= 1 # need a smaller sum
```
Because the array is sorted, moving `left` strictly increases the sum and moving `right` strictly decreases the sum, guaranteeing $O(N)$ time and $O(1)$ space.
